4e14de0bc7f0a6fc0e33b6","file":"preprints/Short-Egyptian-fractions-September-25-2026/build/elementary.tex","line":7,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"5f4b741062602a47f946287a74117451d92498073c8aef40815c65c4f41eb3fe","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Short-Egyptian-fractions-September-25-2026/build/elementary.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:b17cb59f4161fc2bba6ab06c3e8325e97b640a2de34e14de0bc7f0a6fc0e33b6","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Short-Egyptian-fractions-September-25-2026/build/elementary.tex#L7"},"statement_kind":"proposition","text":"\\label{prop:density}\nThere are absolute constants \\(D_M>1\\), \\(L>0\\), and \\(S_0>1\\) with the\nfollowing property.  Put \\(D_X=D_M+2\\) and \\(D_C=4D_X\\).\nFor every real \\(S\\ge S_0\\) and every integer \\(C\\) satisfying\n\\[\n e^{D_CS}\\le C\\le e^{2D_CS},\n\\]\nthere are an integer \\(M\\) and a set\n\\(G\\subseteq\\{1,\\ldots,\\lfloor X\\rfloor\\}\\), where \\(X=e^{D_XS}\\), such that\n\\[\n e^S<M\\le e^{D_MS},\n \\qquad\n \\bigl|\\{1,\\ldots,\\lfloor X\\rfloor\\}\\setminus G\\bigr|\\le \\frac X8.\n\\]\nFor each \\(u\\in G\\), the fraction \\(u/(MC)\\) is a sum of at most\n\\(L\\log S\\) unit fractions with integer denominators at least \\(2\\).\nRepetitions are allowed."}
